## Repro

Run `pnpm dev:watch` against a paperclip instance with one or more stale `heartbeatRuns` rows (any prior unclean shutdown produces this). Server fully boots, logs `reaped orphaned heartbeat runs` and `startup productivity reconciliation`, then immediately crashes with `Error: write EPIPE` from `node:internal/stream_base_commons:95`.

## Root cause

[`packages/adapter-utils/src/server-utils.ts:2059-2066`](packages/adapter-utils/src/server-utils.ts#L2059-L2066). When a child process is spawned with `opts.stdin` set, the input is written from a `spawnPersistPromise.finally` callback. The check `if (child.killed || stdin.destroyed) return;` is not sufficient — if the child exits *between* the persist promise resolving and the `stdin.write()` call (or its underlying syscall), the write produces an `EPIPE`. No `'error'` listener is attached to `stdin`, so the `EPIPE` becomes an `uncaughtException`.

## Triggering path

1. Reaper completes
2. `startNextQueuedRunForAgent` runs for one of the reaped agents
3. Spawns a tool/adapter command with stdin payload
4. Child exits fast (e.g. `ENOENT`, immediate completion, or signal)
5. `stdin.write` races and `EPIPE`s

## Suggested fix

Attach `stdin.on("error", noop)`, also check `stdin.writable`, and pass a callback to `stdin.write` to capture non-`EPIPE` errors via the existing log error path.

```ts
if (opts.stdin != null && stdin) {
  stdin.on("error", () => {});
  void spawnPersistPromise.finally(() => {
    if (child.killed || stdin.destroyed || !stdin.writable) return;
    stdin.write(opts.stdin as string, (err) => {
      if (err && (err as NodeJS.ErrnoException).code !== "EPIPE") {
        onLogError(err, runId, "failed to write stdin to child");
      }
    });
    stdin.end();
  });
}
```

## Summary

When the Paperclip server loses its in-memory handle to a child `claude --print` process but the child PID is still alive, `reapOrphanedRuns()` correctly marks the run as `process_detached`. However it then unconditionally `continue`s — **it never schedules a kill**, no matter how long the run stays silent. Recovery currently requires a board-level `POST /api/heartbeat-runs/{runId}/cancel`, which itself requires `assertBoard(req)` — making it inaccessible to the agent and effectively locking the company until a human intervenes.

We hit this on 2026-05-05: a CTO agent run hung silently for ~15 days, blocking all downstream agents.

## Root Cause

In `server/src/services/heartbeat.ts → reapOrphanedRuns()`:

```ts
if (processPidAlive) {
  if (run.errorCode !== DETACHED_PROCESS_ERROR_CODE) {
    // Mark as process_detached (correct)
    ...
  }
  continue;  // <-- BUG: already-detached runs are never terminated
}
