## Summary

`findMentionedAgents` in `server/src/services/issues.ts` resolves explicit
`agent://<uuid>` mention IDs from comment/issue bodies and returns them as
wake targets **without verifying** the UUIDs actually exist in the `agents`
table for the issue's company. Hallucinated UUIDs leak straight into
`enqueueWakeup` and produce orphaned wake attempts.

Filed by Wachter Intelligence (Marcel Wachter, paperclip company id
`5140e458-f9ce-444f-b516-701f85d08307`) — we saw an agent post
``[@Felix Strauss](agent://2803ddcf-95e5-4c7a-aa2b-94cf06aa5a83)`` (wrong
name — Hartmann is correct — and a fabricated UUID; our real Felix is
`2803ddcf-888b-4cbf-8dad-de05ece364f5`). The wake-on-comment path
`server/src/routes/issues.ts:1877` / `:2493` then tried to wake the
non-existent agent.

## Reproduction

1. Post an issue comment with body containing
   `[@Anyone](agent://00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000)`.
2. Server resolves the UUID via `extractAgentMentionIds(body)` and
   adds it to `resolved` unconditionally.
3. `findMentionedAgents` returns the hallucinated UUID.
4. The caller (wake-on-comment route) tries to enqueue a wakeup for an
   agent that doesn't exist or belongs to a different company.

Code path (server v0.3.1, file as installed):

```
server/src/services/issues.ts:2377-2398   findMentionedAgents
server/src/routes/issues.ts:1877          mentionedIds = await svc.findMentionedAgents(...)
server/src/routes/issues.ts:2493          (issue update path)
```

## Proposed fix

Filter `resolved` against the `agents` query result so only IDs that
**belong to the same company** survive. The query already loads all
agents for the company; we just have to use the id set.

```ts
// server/src/services/issues.ts — findMentionedAgents

findMentionedAgents: async (companyId: string, body: string) => {
  const re = /\B@([^\s@,!?.]+)/g;
  const tokens = new Set<string>();
  let m: RegExpExecArray | null;
  while ((m = re.exec(body)) !== null) {
    const normalized = normalizeAgentMentionToken(m[1]);
    if (normalized) tokens.add(normalized.toLowerCase());
  }

  const explicitAgentMentionIds = extractAgentMentionIds(body);
  if (tokens.size === 0 && explicitAgentMentionIds.length === 0) return [];

  const rows = await db.select({ id: agents.id, name: agents.name })
    .from(agents).where(eq(agents.companyId, companyId));
  const validIds = new Set(rows.map((r) => r.id));

  const resolved = new Set<string>();
  // Only keep explicit mention IDs that actually belong to this company.
  for (const id of explicitAgentMentionIds) {
    if (validIds.has(id)) {
      resolved.add(id);
    } else {
      logger.warn(
        { companyId, hallucinatedAgentId: id },
        "findMentionedAgents: ignoring agent:// mention with unknown id",
      );
    }
  }
  for (const agent of rows) {
    if (tokens.has(agent.name.toLowerCase())) {
      resolved.add(agent.id);
    }
  }
  return [...resolved];
},
```

(Logger import path matches the rest of the file — adjust as needed if
the file uses a different logger.)

