## Summary

When a brand-new user signs up via a `company_join` invite link, `POST /invites/{token}/accept` is never called server-side. The user ends up signed in but with no `company_memberships` row, landing on the `CloudAccessGate` ("No company access. This account is signed in, but it does not have an active company membership or instance-admin access on this Paperclip instance.").

This affects every single non-bootstrap, non-agent invite, not just edge cases.

## Repro

1. Stand up an authenticated/private Paperclip instance.
2. Bootstrap a CEO account.
3. As CEO, navigate to `/{prefix}/company/settings/invites` and create a `company_join` invite with `role=owner` (or any role).
4. Open the invite URL in a clean browser session (incognito).
5. Fill out the sign-up form and submit.
6. Observe: sign-up succeeds, user is now authenticated, but the page renders `CloudAccessGate` instead of completing the invite acceptance.

Server logs confirm the issue:

```
INFO  POST /api/auth/sign-up/email 200
(no subsequent POST /invites/{token}/accept)
```

The `invites.accepted_at` column stays NULL, and no `company_memberships` row is created for the new user.

## Root cause

`ui/src/pages/InviteLanding.tsx`, the `authMutation.onSuccess` handler returns early for any non-bootstrap invite:

```js
// ui/src/pages/InviteLanding.tsx (current)
